{
  "id": "29_statement_mark",
  "function": "statement_mark",
  "note": "The mark a capital account statement gives, by hand (docs/08 section 12, rule 12.1). Lines are as read, in the unit read, and converted to dollars first; the tie tolerance is 1 for dollars, 2,500 for thousands, 25,000 for millions and 25,000,000 for billions, and contributions differ beyond 2% of the record. Case 1, worked example 1: our own account in US$ millions, 18.42 + 2.00 - 0.35 + 0.87 = 20.94, so the lines add up and S = 20,940,000; contributions to date of 12.40 agree with the 12,400,000.00 on record (worked example 8). Cases 2 and 3, worked example 2: a net gain of 0.89 leaves the lines 20,000 apart (inside 25,000, they tie) and 0.92 leaves them 50,000 apart (they do not); S is unchanged. Case 4, worked example 3: the whole vehicle at a 25% share, 83.76 x 0.25 = 20.94; our part of the lines is 18,420,000, 2,000,000 and 350,000 and of the contributions to date 49.60 x 0.25 = 12,400,000. Case 5, worked example 8: a statement showing 30.00 against 12,400,000 is 17,600,000 over, 141.93548387%. Cases 6 and 7: lines 25,000.00 apart are on the tolerance and tie; 25,000.01 apart do not. Cases 8 and 9: read in dollars, 1.00 apart ties and 1.01 does not (fixture 11's tolerance). Cases 10 and 11: read in thousands, 2,000 apart ties and 3,000 does not. Case 12: read in billions, 10,000,000 apart ties. Case 13: four lines in thousands and the ending balance in millions; the coarsest unit read sets the tolerance (25,000), and the contributions to date, read in dollars, are no part of it. Case 14: no net gain stated, so there is no answer on the tie and S stands. Case 15: no ending balance, with a share of 150%: the first reason is given, and the contributions are not checked because the share is out of range. Cases 16 and 17: an ending balance of zero, and one of -500,000 with a share of zero: both are non_positive_balance. Cases 18 to 20: a share of 0, of -25% and of 100.01% is out of range; our part of no line is worked out. Case 21: a share of exactly 1 is in range: S is the balance, and the lines were not read as our own account. Case 22: 1,000,000.01 x 0.3333 = 333,300.003333, so 333,300.00; our part of the beginning balance is 900,000 x 0.3333 = 299,970.00 and of the contributions 33,330.00. Case 23: 100.01 x 0.5 = 50.005, half a cent, rounds up to 50.01. Case 24: 0.01 x 0.1 = 0.001 is under half a cent: no value (value_not_positive). Case 25: nothing on record, so the contributions are not checked. Cases 26 to 28: 12,648,000 is 2% over the record and 12,152,000 2% under, both on the edge and agreeing; a cent over the upper edge is 0.0200000008 and differs. Cases 29 and 30: against a record of 1,000,000,000.00, 1,020,000,000.04 is 0.02000000004 and travels as 0.02 (they agree: the check is judged on the percent as it travels); 1,020,000,000.05 travels as 0.0200000001 and differs. Case 31: contributions to date of 6.20 are half the record, -50%: they differ.",
